  "description": "Two storey rear extension; external alterations",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;; line-height: 20px;&quot;&gt;The proposed two-storey rear extension, by reason of its scale, bulk and design, would form an inappropriate and unduly obtrusive addition that is incongruous with the original dwelling. The development would result in a cumulative overdevelopment of the site, failing to respect the character, proportions and appearance of the host property and the visual amenities of the surrounding area. As such, the proposal would be contrary to the high-quality design objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021–2041), and the relevant provisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed two storey rear extension, by reason of its scale, depth and proximity\r\nto the shared boundary, would breach the 45-degree guideline when assessed from\r\nthe nearest habitable room window of No. 62A. As a result, the development\r\nwould give rise to an unacceptable loss of light and an increased sense of\r\noverbearing enclosure and tunnelling effect to that neighbouring occupier, to the detriment of their\r\nresidential amenity. The proposal is therefore considered to result in a\r\nharmful impact on neighbouring living conditions and is contrary to the\r\nhigh-quality design objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework\r\n(2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local\r\nPlan (2021–2041), and the relevant provisions of the adopted Harrow\r\nSupplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
